Here’s a simple example of a “flip‑card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
Copy the HTML and CSS into your page (or into a CodePen) and watch the card flip.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* Container holding the card */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The inner wrapper that actually flips */
.card-inner {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3D space */
}

/* Flip the card on hover */
.card:hover .card-inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front and back faces */
.card-front,
.card-back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide backside when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front face styling */
.card-front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

/* Back face styling – rotated 180° so it starts hidden */
.card-back {
  background: #fafafa;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* Start flipped */
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-inner">
    <div class="card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-back">
      <h3>Back Content</h3>
      <p>This is the content that appears after the card flips.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

**How it works**

1. `.card` sets up a 3D context with `perspective`.  
2. `.card-inner` holds both sides and has `transform-style: preserve-3d` so its children keep their 3D positions.  
3. On hover, we rotate `.card-inner` 180° around the Y‑axis.  
4. Each side (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) uses `backface-visibility: hidden` so the hidden side isn’t visible.  
5. The back face is initially rotated 180° so it lines up correctly when the container flips.

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add images inside the front/back divs to suit your design!
